<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Côtes-d'Armor</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Côtes-d'Armor is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">department</a> of Brittany in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, on the coast of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/english-channel">English Channel</a>, with its prefecture at Saint-Brieuc. Created in 1790 as Côtes-du-Nord, it took its present name in 1990. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iron-age">Iron Age</a> and Roman period its lands were held by the Coriosolites in the east and the Osismii in the west.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cotes-darmor.jpg" alt="Côtes-d'Armor" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pr%C3%A9fecture_des_C%C3%B4tes-d%27Armor_%C3%A0_Saint-Brieuc.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
